  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.1: the first published release of the 0.3 line; 0.3.0 was tagged but not published, and the library is unchanged since that tag. 0.3.0: breaking: Protocol is renamed NoiseProtocol, the name used by the Swift, Kotlin, Flutter, and React Native packages released from the same repository tag. KeyPair.PublicKey returns a copy on every read. A low-order peer public key (all-zero DH output) now throws CryptographicException and ends the handshake. A tag mismatch throws AuthenticationTagMismatchException with the fixed message \"The authentication tag did not match.\"; psk modifier digits must be ASCII digits without a sign; an empty protocol name reports \"'' is not a valid Noise protocol name.\" The NuGet README is the C# package README under dotnet/. 0.2.0: every Noise handshake pattern (one-way, fundamental, deferred) with psk modifiers; Curve448; BLAKE2s/BLAKE2b; one-directional Transport for one-way patterns; the full cacophony and snow vector suites (1,352 vectors) run with none skipped.",
